WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.800
Cheap-Drive: quote requests, post driver gigs, and deliver at least 90% on time.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:12.800
Prototype. Test. Loop. Repeat. Alpha: 677 runs, formula quotes. Beta: 268, trust and fee timing. Gamma: 242, notes and two-car gigs. Delta: 303, rescue windows.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:19.800
Beta: filter requests, price dealer trust, time gig fees, and meet deadlines. Fees stay flat while pickup is unavailable, then rise from 0.80× to 1.50× as usable time runs out.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:25.800
Find what broke. Inspect the note, pickup window, and outcome alongside the report and six-run switcher. The order shown is an illustrative example.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:33.800
1,492 practice runs, including failures. Ranked shares: Alpha 84.6%, Beta 88.1%, Gamma 97.9%, and Delta 99.0%.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:40.800
First Gamma holdout: +€830 gross margin per week versus Beta across eight new practice weeks. Seven of eight ranked; worst on time was 89.96%, below the 90% gate.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:47.800
Gamma: notes and two-car gigs. +€2,031 gross margin per week versus Beta across eight new practice weeks. Eight of eight ranked; worst on time was 96.95%.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:54.800
Delta: rescue stranded orders. +€682 gross margin per week versus Gamma across eleven paired practice weeks. Eleven of eleven ranked; worst on time was 93.7%.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:59.800
Win the right work. Deliver it.
